  "configuration_id": "config_049",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_037, scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted, 0.706 acc) establishes a strong multimodal configuration, and scvi_n200 has shown a modest edge over pca_n2000. However, the scgpt RNA encoder is completely untested across all experiments, representing the largest remaining uncertainty in the design space. Question: config_049 (scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile) isolates the RNA encoder as the only variable changed from the current best, directly testing whether scgpt can match or exceed scvi_n200 in the strongest known multimodal context. Why this is the best use of the next experiment: With a limited budget, testing an entirely unexplored encoder in the best-known configuration provides the highest information gain per experiment—either confirming scvi_n200 as the optimal RNA encoder (reducing search space) or revealing a superior alternative that could further improve performance. The other untested dimensions (transformer aggregation, singleprofile) already have moderate negative evidence from prior runs, making them lower-priority uncertainties compared to the completely unknown scgpt performance."
}

